{
  "_about": "Gold query set for the 10-book indexed corpus (Frankenstein, A Tale of Two Cities, Around the World in Eighty Days, The Call of the Wild, Pride and Prejudice, The Adventures of Sherlock Holmes, The Works of Edgar Allan Poe Vol. 1, Moby Dick, Ulysses, The Great Gatsby). 5 per book, sharpness 1 (very unique to the book) -> 5 (generic archetype). Each entry simulates a distilled LLM query frame: a general-register summary (present tense, no proper names, feeling words only in descriptors) plus the decomposed frame (subject/verb/object/setting), a combined `svos` clause synthesized from that frame (feeds the svos multivector channel), and a guessed descriptor vibe. Used to probe retrieval precision falloff as a query gets more general.",
